{"url": "https://theranetrix.com/", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en-US", "text": "Clinical Decision Support | Wellesley, MA | TheraNetrix, Inc.\nTheraNetrix, Inc. delivers AI-powered clinical decision support and patient engagement tools for pain management in Wellesley, MA, and beyond.\nTheraNetrix, Inc. delivers AI-powered clinical decision support and patient engagement tools for pain management in Wellesley, MA, and beyond.\nClinical Decision Support | Wellesley, MA | TheraNetrix, Inc. Home Services TheraNetrix CDSS MobileNetrix Patient Application Clinical Trial Support / Studies About About TheraNetrix, Inc. Management Clinician Advisory Panel News & Events Contact Us Home Services TheraNetrix CDSS MobileNetrix Patient Application Clinical Trial Support / Studies About About TheraNetrix, Inc. Management Clinician Advisory Panel News & Events Contact Us Clinical Decision Support System for Pain Management TheraNetrix, Inc. is transforming the future of pain management through intelligent, data-driven healthcare solutions. Our TheraNetrix™ Clinical Decision Support System (CDSS) is powered by advanced mathematical modeling techniques, informed by artificial intelligence and digital twin technology, with patient-centered, real-time input. We help clinicians personalize treatments, improve patient outcomes, and deliver safer, more effective care for chronic and acute pain. Smarter Pain Management Starts Here We bring together the patient-facing MobileNetrix™ app and the clinician-based Prescribing Support Tool of In Silico Biosciences in a user-friendly, intuitive platform to empower physicians with predictive, evidence-based combination drug therapy recommendations tailored to patients needs. Informed by AI and Digital Twin Technology TheraNetrix CDSS is driven by an innovative, highly integrative, and multidisciplinary Quantitative Systems Pharmacology (QSP) engine that employs patient data, clinical history, and social determinants of health. Our proprietary Digital Twin models simulate real-world patient outcomes, allowing for safer, more precise care decisions. Engaging Patients Every Step of the Way MobileNetrix™ facilitates communication between providers and patients through tools for symptom tracking, medication monitoring, goal setting, education, and psychological support. Designed for both clinical use and research, the platform strengthens regimen adherence, encourages self-management, and improves long-term health outcomes. Built by Experts, Backed by Science Founded in 2025, TheraNetrix is led by a team of healthcare innovators, researchers, and industry leaders. With support from our partners and advisory panel, we aim to redefine what’s possible in the treatment of persistent pain. Explore Our Services TheraNetrix CDSS Leverage advanced AI and Digital Twin modeling to guide safe and personalized drug therapy decisions. Read More MobileNetrix Patient Application Strengthen patient engagement and self-management with real-time communication tools. Read MOre Clinical Trial Support / Studies Deploy scalable tools for regulatory-compliant studies, data analysis, and population health management. Read More Why Choose TheraNetrix? Grounded in real-world data and evidence-based care Powered by AI and Digital Twin modeling Built for clinical use, scalable for research Enhances both provider workflows and patient outcomes About Learn how TheraNetrix combines technology and clinical expertise to improve healthcare outcomes. Read More Services Explore our healthcare technology, clinical research, patient engagement, and consulting services. Read MOre News & Events View TheraNetrix in action through our healthcare solutions, programs, and research initiatives. Read More Contact Us Get in touch with TheraNetrix, Inc. for personalized healthcare solutions and support. read more Discover a new paradigm in pain management today Contact us Address TheraNetrix Inc. 17 Brook Street, Wellesley MA 02482 Contact Phone: 617 763 7457 | 781 235 1995 Email: info@theranetrix.com Services About News & Events Contact Us More links Legal notice Privacy policy LinkedIn This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program under grant agreement No 848068 © 2026 TheraNetrix, Inc."}
