{"url": "https://theranetrix.com/about-us/", "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "language_hint": "en-US", "text": "About Us | Leadership & Innovation in Pain Management | Wellesley, MA | TheraNetrix, Inc.\nMeet the team behind TheraNetrix, Inc. in Wellesley, MA—pioneering AI-driven pain care through clinical decision support, patient technology, and expert leadership.\nMeet the team behind TheraNetrix, Inc. in Wellesley, MA—pioneering AI-driven pain care through clinical decision support, patient technology, and expert leadership.\nAbout Us | Leadership & Innovation in Pain Management | Wellesley, MA | TheraNetrix, Inc. Home Services TheraNetrix CDSS MobileNetrix Patient Application Clinical Trial Support / Studies About About TheraNetrix, Inc. Management Clinician Advisory Panel News & Events Contact Us Home Services TheraNetrix CDSS MobileNetrix Patient Application Clinical Trial Support / Studies About About TheraNetrix, Inc. Management Clinician Advisory Panel News & Events Contact Us About TheraNetrix, Inc. Founded in 2025, TheraNetrix, Inc. is a digital health company on a mission to revolutionize how chronic and acute pain are treated. By combining artificial intelligence, Digital Twin modeling, and clinical decision support, we provide tools that improve outcomes for patients while supporting physicians with actionable, evidence-based insights. Vision Vision Vision To transform pain management worldwide, empowering medical practitioners to enhance patient outcomes and advancing health equity Mission We are committed to advancing evidence-based care, improving quality of life, and supporting the healthcare system with an artificial intelligence-informed clinical decision support system for safe, effective, and individualized pain management treatments. Management Edgar Ross, MD – Chairman & Chief Medical Officer Edgar Ross, MD, is Chairman and Chief Medical Officer of TheraNetrix. Dr. Ross is a board-certified anesthesiologist and pain management specialist. He is a renowned pain expert, specializing in areas such as chronic pain, spinal conditions, and vascular pain. Dr. Ross has been involved in medical innovation, including the development of devices for patients with neuromuscular disorders and the formation of digital health companies focused on pain and mental health treatment. He is the author of over 100 peer-reviewed articles. Dr. Ross is the co-developer of the MobileNetrix patient-facing application, which he invented and co-developed when he was Director of the Pain Management Center at Brigham and Women’s Hospital. TheraNetrix has licensed MobileNetrix from Massachusetts General Brigham for use in the TheraNetrix Clinical Decision Support System. David Guydan – President & CEO David Guydan is President and CEO of TheraNetrix. He brings critical leadership and commercialization expertise to the TheraNetrix venture. Mr. Guydan has extensive experience in creating new businesses, achieving business turnarounds, and business development for sustained growth. His experience extends to articulating corporate vision, formulating strategic plans, leading business/product development, launching integrated marketing programs, and effectively utilizing business resources to achieve immediate and long-term results. His industry experience includes biotechnology services, electronic payment systems, institutional investments, and information services with organizations ranging from start-ups to money center banks. He holds a BA in economics from the University of Pittsburgh and an MBA from Harvard Business School. Robert Jamison, PhD – Senior Scientific Advisor Robert Jamison, PhD, is Senior Scientific Advisor of TheraNetrix, Inc. Dr. Jamison is a Professor at Harvard Medical School with appointments in the Departments of Anesthesiology, Psychiatry, and Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation. He is a clinical psychologist with principal offices in the Brigham and Women’s Pain Management Center. His past research has focused on the examination of predictors of opioid abuse in chronic pain patients. He has been a principal investigator on several NIH-funded projects, has been on the Editorial Boards of five scientific journals, and has held board and leadership positions in many regional, national, and international pain organizations. He has authored two books and over 300 peer-reviewed articles in the areas of behavioral medicine and chronic pain. Together with Dr. Ross, he is the inventor and co-developer of the MobileNetrix patient-facing application Robert Carr – Senior Advisor Robert Carr is Senior Advisor to TheraNetrix, Inc. and Chairman and CEO of In Silico Biosciences, Inc. (ISB). Mr. Carr is a seasoned entrepreneur focused on maximizing the effective use of human intellectual capital. In 2000, after identifying computational neuropharmacology as the opportunity for such development in the pharmaceutical industry, Mr. Carr began successfully organizing and developing ISB. ISB uses its advanced mathematical modeling techniques, combined with the academic discipline of computational neurosciences, to focus on pharmaceutical research and drug development. In 2020, ISB joined nine European institutions in a five-year European Union-funded pain relief project in which the ISB computational models were employed for identifying optimal, personalized, combination drug treatment of pain patients. The resulting ISB Pain Management Service drives the Prescribing Support Tool, which is licensed to TheraNetrix for its TheraNetrix Clinical Decision Support System. Mr. Carr has a BS in mathematics from the University of California, Riverside, and an MBA from Harvard Business School. Clinician Advisory Panel The Clinician Advisory Panel was formed to collaborate in the development of a “Prescribing Support Tool” designed to advance state-of-the-art combination drug treatment options for chronic pain patients. The Prescribing Support Tool is a user-friendly computer-based aid in the hands of clinicians for improved patient outcomes and greater patient satisfaction. The Tool is integrated into the TheraNetrix Clinical Decision Support System as the clinician interface, which, combined with the MobileNetrix patient-facing application and informed by AI and Digital Twin computer models for personalized medicine, revolutionizes evidence-based treatment of patients with chronic pain. We are grateful to these members of the Panel who have offered their expertise and input in the creation of a valuable new resource that will support clinicians’ own best practices in prescribing safe and effective patient-specific combination treatment options for chronic pain. We are grateful for the support and insights of our advisory panel: Edgar L. Ross, MD (Founding Clinician) Gregory Acampora, MD Ali Ebrahimi, MD Keith Fragoza, MD Joseph A. Hanak, MD Richard S. Harold, DMD, JD Janet D. Pearl, MD Discover how our team is shaping the future of pain management Contact Us Address TheraNetrix Inc. 17 Brook Street, Wellesley MA 02482 Contact Phone: 617 763 7457 | 781 235 1995 Email: info@theranetrix.com Services About News & Events Contact Us More links Legal notice Privacy policy LinkedIn This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program under grant agreement No 848068 © 2026 TheraNetrix, Inc."}
